eRestoreSpan","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"TreeRestoreSpan carries a tree node run from a single deletion, addressed","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"by TreeNodeID identity, for identity-preserving Tree undo\/redo. Unlike the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"text RestoreSpan (flat offsets), a tree span records the node’s structure","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(type\/attrs) and its position anchors, because in a tree id-order is not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sibling-order: left_sibling_id and right_sibling_id are redundant external","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"boundary anchors of the deleted run, so restore can reconstruct the run’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"internal order from the op’s own spans and needs only one surviving","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"boundary to place it. value\/attributes are a deep copy so a GC-purged node","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"can be recreated.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Yorkie_V1_TreeRestoreSpan","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"Yorkie_V1_TreeRestoreSpan","role":"symbol"},"doc://Yorkie/documentation/Yorkie/Yorkie_V1_TreeRestoreSpan/merge(contiguousBytes:extensions:partial:options:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Yorkie\/documentation\/Yorkie\/Yorkie_V1_TreeRestoreSpan\/merge(contiguousBytes:extensions:partial:options:)","kind":"symbol","title":"merge(contiguousBytes:extensions:partial:options:)","url":"\/documentation\/yorkie\/yorkie_v1_treerestorespan\/merge(contiguousbytes:extensions:partial:options:)","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"merge","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bytes","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"contiguousBytes","kind":"external